n\n### Steps\n\n1. **`internal/gitx/local.go` (new method)** `func (g *Git) ListTree(ctx context.Context, dir, rev, prefix string) ([]string, error)`: runs `ls-tree -r -z --name-only --full-tree <rev> -- <prefix>` with `--git-dir=gitDirOf(dir)` and `--literal-pathspecs`, same path validation as `FileAt` (reject empty, leading `/`, `..`). Returns repo-relative paths. Reason: nothing lists a directory today, and the committer takes file paths. Add a test next to the existing gitx tests using `gitx/gittest` fixtures.\n2. **`internal/janitor/janitor.go` (new package)**, modelled on `internal/scanner/stale/stale.go`:\n   - `const Name = \"janitor\"`, `Retention = 90 * 24 * time.Hour`, `Interval = 24 * time.Hour`.\n   - Interfaces: `Reader` (`SearchIssues`, `GetIssue` from `github.Reader`), `Committer` (`Commit(ctx, committer.Request) (committer.Result, error)`), `Tree` (`Dirs(ctx) ([]int, error)` and `Files(ctx, issue int) ([]string, error)`, or one func type), and a `now func() time.Time`.\n   - `type Janitor struct{...}`; `New(...)`; `Name`, `Interval(*config.Resolved)`, `Claims() bool` returns true (it writes main, so pause stops it), `Tick(ctx, controller.Env)`.\n   - Monthly cadence: keep an in-memory `lastRun`; `Tick` returns nil unless 30 days have passed since the last completed pass (first tick after start always runs). The pass is idempotent, so losing the timestamp on restart only costs one extra scan.\n   - Pass: list the `.ard/<n>/` directories on the fetched main (step 1; numeric names only, so `config.yaml`, `scanners/`, `triage/`, `workers/`, `reviewers/` are never candidates). Search `is:issue is:closed closed:<cutoff` with `SearchOpts{Max: 1000}` for candidates, and keep only issue numbers that have a directory. For each, re-fetch with `GetIssue` and require `State == closed`, `!IsPR`, `ClosedAt != nil` and `now - ClosedAt > Retention` (this guards reopened or racing issues). Skip any issue carrying `labels.Hold` or the `ard:keep` label, and log the skip.\n   - Delete: for each eligible issue, build `committer.Request{Issue: n, Stage: \"janitor\", Role: \"prune\", Summary: \"prune closed issue directory\", Files: [{Path, Delete: true}...]}`, chunked to `committer.MaxFiles` per request. Commit only through the `Committer` interface; a guard error or conflict is logged and counted, and the loop moves to the next issue. Return a joined error at the end as `stale` does.\n3. **`internal/servecmd/janitor.go` (new)** `func janitorLoop(w *wiring) controller.Loop`: wire `w.Reader`, `w.mainCommitter()` (the shared `lazyCommitter`; do not build a second committer) and a tree lister reading the controller clone at the main head that the committer lane fetches (check `internal/committer/refs.go` for the ref name; if none is readable outside the lane, add a small `committer.Committer` method that lists a prefix at the fetched head rather than re-fetching in the loop). Dry-run is honoured because the committer goes through `effects`.\n4. **`internal/servecmd/serve.go`**: add `janitor.Name` to `knownLoops` (before `\"reaper\"`) and `loops = append(loops, janitorLoop(w))` in `registerLoops`. Update the `--loops` docs string in `internal/cli/cmd_serve.go` if it lists loop names. Check the existing loops-selection tests in `internal/servecmd` that assert the full list.\n5. **Docs**: `docs/proposal.md` (the audit-trail paragraph near \"Directories outlive their issues\", the `--loops` list in the executor section, and the commit-message note) to say how the janitor runs: the 30-day cadence, the 90-day cutoff, the `ard:keep` and `ard:hold` skips, the commit as `ard(janitor:prune)`. Add `internal/janitor/` to the layout list in `CLAUDE.md`. Note: `CLAUDE.md` is a protected path, so that edit makes the PR wait for a human approval.\n\n### Test plan\n\nCommand: `make test` (`go test ./...`), plus `make lint`. Tests use `github/fake` and a recording `Committer` fake.\n- `TestJanitorPrunesOldClosed` (`internal/janitor/janitor_test.go`): issue closed 91 days ago with dir files `.ard/7/a.md`, `.ard/7/logs/x.log`. Expect one request with `Issue: 7` and a `Delete` entry per file.\n- `TestJanitorKeepsRecent`: closed 89 days ago. Expect no commit.\n- `TestJanitorSkipsOpenAndReopened`: open issue, and an issue the search returned but `GetIssue` shows reopened. Expect no commit.\n- `TestJanitorNeverTouchesNonIssueDirs`: tree contains `.ard/config.yaml`, `.ard/triage/lead/...`, `.ard/workers/...`. Expect none in any request.\n- `TestJanitorSkipsKeepAndHold`: labelled issues skipped.\n- `TestJanitorChunksOver256Files`: 300 files give two requests, both `Issue: 7`.\n- `TestJanitorContinuesAfterCommitError`: first issue's commit fails; the second is still pruned and `Tick` returns an error.\n- `TestJanitorMonthlyGate`: a second `Tick` within 30 days does nothing; one after 30 days runs.\n- `TestJanitorClaimsAndName`: `Claims()` is true; `Name()` is `janitor`.\n- `TestListTree` (`internal/gitx`): nested files, a missing prefix (empty result), a bad path (error).\n- servecmd: the unknown-loop and `registerLoops` tests include `janitor`.\nEdge cases: an issue with no directory (nothing to do); a PR with the same number space; `ClosedAt` nil; a dir already deleted (committer treats absent delete paths as fine, so the commit is a NoOp).\n\n### Risk\n\nMedium. It deletes files from `main` through the committer, whose `CheckPath` already limits writes to `.ard/<issue#>/` for the request's own issue, so config and role directories cannot be hit even by a bug. Files touched are not in `merge.protected_paths` except `CLAUDE.md` (step 5, human approval needed). It adds a new background loop and changes `knownLoops` (public `--loops` interface). Race with a reopened issue is handled by the re-fetch. No migrations or concurrency beyond sharing the existing lazy main committer.\n\n### Size\n\nM (about 250 changed lines including tests). Files: `internal/gitx/local.go` (+test), `internal/janitor/janitor.go` and `janitor_test.go` (new), `internal/servecmd/janitor.go` (new), `internal/servecmd/serve.go` (+tests), `docs/proposal.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, possibly `internal/committer/` (listing helper).\n22:diff --git a/CLAUDE.md b/CLAUDE.md\n25:+++ b/CLAUDE.md\n34:diff --git a/docs/proposal.md b/docs/proposal.md\n37:+++ b/docs/proposal.md\n56:diff --git a/internal/cli/cmd_serve.go b/internal/cli/cmd_serve.go\n59:+++ b/internal/cli/cmd_serve.go\n68:diff --git a/internal/github/fake/fake.go b/internal/github/fake/fake.go\n71:+++ b/internal/github/fake/fake.go\n93:diff --git a/internal/gitx/export_test.go b/internal/gitx/export_test.go\n96:+++ b/internal/gitx/export_test.go\n140:diff --git a/internal/gitx/local.go b/internal/gitx/local.go\n143:+++ b/internal/gitx/local.go\n170:diff --git a/internal/janitor/janitor.go b/internal/janitor/janitor.go\n174:+++ b/internal/janitor/janitor.go\n363:diff --git a/internal/janitor/janitor_test.go b/internal/janitor/janitor_test.go\n367:+++ b/internal/janitor/janitor_test.go\n547:diff --git a/internal/servecmd/janitor.go b/internal/servecmd/janitor.go\n551:+++ b/internal/servecmd/janitor.go\n584:diff --git a/internal/servecmd/loops_test.go b/internal/servecmd/loops_test.go\n587:+++ b/internal/servecmd/loops_test.go\n606:diff --git a/internal/servecmd/rebuild_test.go b/internal/servecmd/rebuild_test.go\n609:+++ b/internal/servecmd/rebuild_test.go\n621:diff --git a/internal/servecmd/serve.go b/internal/servecmd/serve.go\n624:+++ b/internal/servecmd/serve.go\n// Package janitor prunes the .ard/<issue#>/ directories of issues closed\n// long ago (#61). Git history keeps the audit trail. It is a plain controller\n// loop: no slot, executor or worktree. Every deletion goes through the main\n// committer, whose path guard confines a request to its own issue's\n// directory, so .ard/config.yaml and the role directories can never be hit.\npackage janitor\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"log/slog\"\n\t\"regexp\"\n\t\"sort\"\n\t\"strconv\"\n\t\"sync\"\n\t\"time\"\n\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/committer\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/config\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/controller\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/github\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/labels\"\n)\n\nconst (\n\tName = \"janitor\"\n\t// Retention is how long an issue must have been closed before its\n\t// directory is pruned.\n\tRetention = 90 * 24 * time.Hour\n\t// Interval is how often the loop wakes; Period is how often it works.\n\tInterval = 24 * time.Hour\n\tPeriod   = 30 * 24 * time.Hour\n)\n\n// Reader is the read side, satisfied by github.Reader.\ntype Reader interface {\n\tSearchIssues(ctx context.Context, q string, o github.SearchOpts) ([]github.Issue, error)\n\tGetIssue(ctx context.Context, n int) (github.Issue, error)\n}\n\n// Committer commits to main, satisfied by the shared main committer.\ntype Committer interface {\n\tCommit(ctx context.Context, req committer.Request) (committer.Result, error)\n}\n\n// Tree lists every file path under .ard/ at the latest main.\ntype Tree func(ctx context.Context) ([]string, error)\n\n// Janitor is the pruning loop.\ntype Janitor struct {\n\tgh   Reader\n\tcm   Committer\n\ttree Tree\n\tnow  func() time.Time\n\n\tmu      sync.Mutex\n\tlastRun time.Time\n}\n\nvar _ controller.Loop = (*Janitor)(nil)\n\n// New returns a Janitor; a nil now means time.Now.\nfunc New(gh Reader, cm Committer, tree Tree, now func() time.Time) *Janitor {\n\tif now == nil {\n\t\tnow = time.Now\n\t}\n\treturn &Janitor{gh: gh, cm: cm, tree: tree, now: now}\n}\n\nfunc (j *Janitor) Name() string                            { return Name }\nfunc (j *Janitor) Interval(*config.Resolved) time.Duration { return Interval }\n\n// Claims is true so that pause stops pruning.\nfunc (j *Janitor) Claims() bool { return true }\n\nvar issueDirRe = regexp.MustCompile(`^\\.ard/([1-9][0-9]*)/`)\n\n// Tick runs a pass when Period has passed since the last completed one. The\n// pass is idempotent, so losing lastRun on a restart costs one extra scan.\nfunc (j *Janitor) Tick(ctx context.Context, env controller.Env) error {\n\tnow := j.now()\n\tj.mu.Lock()\n\tlast := j.lastRun\n\tj.mu.Unlock()\n\tif !last.IsZero() && now.Sub(last) < Period {\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\tif err := j.pass(ctx, env.Log, now); err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tj.mu.Lock()\n\tj.lastRun = now\n\tj.mu.Unlock()\n\treturn nil\n}\n\nfunc (j *Janitor) pass(ctx context.Context, log *slog.Logger, now time.Time) error {\n\tpaths, err := j.tree(ctx)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"janitor: list .ard: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\tfiles := map[int][]string{}\n\tfor _, p := range paths {\n\t\tif m := issueDirRe.FindStringSubmatch(p); m != nil {\n\t\t\tn, _ := strconv.Atoi(m[1])\n\t\t\tfiles[n] = append(files[n], p)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif len(files) == 0 {\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\tcutoff := now.Add(-Retention).UTC().Format(\"2006-01-02\")\n\tcands, err := j.gh.SearchIssues(ctx, \"is:issue is:closed closed:<\"+cutoff, github.SearchOpts{Sort: \"created\", Order: \"asc\", Max: 1000})\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"janitor: search: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\tsort.Slice(cands, func(a, b int) bool { return cands[a].Number < cands[b].Number })\n\n\tvar errs []error\n\tpruned := 0\n\tfor _, c := range cands {\n\t\tfs := files[c.Number]\n\t\tif len(fs) == 0 {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif ctx.Err() != nil {\n\t\t\terrs = append(errs, ctx.Err())\n\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t}\n\t\t// Re-fetch: the issue may have been reopened since the search.\n\t\tcur, err := j.gh.GetIssue(ctx, c.Number)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\terrs = append(errs, fmt.Errorf(\"issue #%d: get: %w\", c.Number, err))\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif cur.State != github.StateClosed || cur.IsPR || cur.ClosedAt == nil || now.Sub(*cur.ClosedAt) <= Retention {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif hasAny(cur.Labels, labels.Hold, labels.Keep) {\n\t\t\tlog.Info(\"janitor skip\", \"issue\", cur.Number, \"reason\", \"hold or keep label\")\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif err := j.prune(ctx, cur.Number, fs); err != nil {\n\t\t\tlog.Error(\"janitor failed\", \"issue\", cur.Number, \"error\", err)\n\t\t\terrs = append(errs, fmt.Errorf(\"issue #%d: %w\", cur.Number, err))\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tpruned++\n\t\tlog.Info(\"janitor pruned\", \"issue\", cur.Number, \"files\", len(fs))\n\t}\n\tif len(errs) > 0 {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"janitor: %d issues failed (%d pruned): %w\", len(errs), pruned, errors.Join(errs...))\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n\nfunc (j *Janitor) prune(ctx context.Context, n int, paths []string) error {\n\tsort.Strings(paths)\n\tfor len(paths) > 0 {\n\t\tk := min(len(paths), committer.MaxFiles)\n\t\tfs := make([]committer.File, k)\n\t\tfor i, p := range paths[:k] {\n\t\t\tfs[i] = committer.File{Path: p, Delete: true}\n\t\t}\n\t\tpaths = paths[k:]\n\t\t_, err := j.cm.Commit(ctx, committer.Request{\n\t\t\tIssue: n, Stage: \"janitor\", Role: \"prune\",\n\t\t\tSummary: \"prune closed issue directory\", Files: fs,\n\t\t})\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n\nfunc hasAny(have []string, want ...string) bool {\n\tfor _, h := range have {\n\t\tfor _, w := range want {\n\t\t\tif h == w {\n\t\t\t\treturn true\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn false\n}\npackage servecmd\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/controller\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/gitx\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/janitor\"\n)\n\n// janitorRef is where the janitor keeps its own fetch of main in the\n// controller clone, apart from the committer lane's ref.\nconst janitorRef = \"refs/ard/janitor/main\"\n\n// janitorLoop builds the janitor loop (#61). It lists .ard/ on a fresh fetch\n// of main and deletes only through the shared main committer.\nfunc janitorLoop(w *wiring) controller.Loop {\n\tg := gitx.New(\"\")\n\ttree := func(ctx context.Context) ([]string, error) {\n\t\tif err := g.FetchRef(ctx, w.Root, w.RemoteURL, \"+refs/heads/main:\"+janitorRef, w.Token); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"fetch main: %w\", err)\n\t\t}\n\t\tsha, err := g.RevParse(ctx, w.Root, janitorRef)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn nil, err\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn g.ListTree(ctx, w.Root, sha, \".ard\")\n\t}\n\treturn janitor.New(w.Reader, w.mainCommitter(), tree, nil)\n}\npackage gitx\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"errors\"\ndiff --git a/internal/github/fake/fake.go b/internal/github/fake/fake.go\nindex 02af575..ace8f8c 100644\n--- a/internal/github/fake/fake.go\n+++ b/internal/github/fake/fake.go\n@@ -1114,6 +1114,10 @@ func parseSearch(q string) (searchTerms, error) {\n \t\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"unsupported qualifier in:%s\", v)\n \t\t\t}\n \t\tcase \"label\":\n+\t\tcase \"closed\":\n+\t\t\tif _, err := time.Parse(\"2006-01-02\", strings.TrimPrefix(v, \"<\")); err != nil || !strings.HasPrefix(v, \"<\") {\n+\t\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"unsupported qualifier closed:%s (want closed:<YYYY-MM-DD)\", v)\n+\t\t\t}\n \t\tdefault:\n \t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"unsupported qualifier %q\", k)\n \t\t}\n@@ -1152,6 +1156,9 @@ func (ts searchTerms) match(it *item) bool {\n \t\t\t}\n \t\tcase \"label\":\n \t\t\tok = hasLabel(it.issue.Labels, t.value)\n+\t\tcase \"closed\":\n+\t\t\tday, _ := time.Parse(\"2006-01-02\", strings.TrimPrefix(t.value, \"<\"))\n+\t\t\tok = it.issue.ClosedAt != nil && it.issue.ClosedAt.UTC().Before(day)\n \t\t}\n \t\tif ok == t.neg {\n \t\t\treturn false\ndiff --git a/internal/gitx/local.go b/internal/gitx/local.go\nindex db07fe5..594f5b8 100644\n--- a/internal/gitx/local.go\n+++ b/internal/gitx/local.go\n@@ -348,6 +348,25 @@ func (g *Git) FileAt(ctx context.Context, dir, rev, path string, maxBytes int64)\n \treturn []byte(blob), true, nil\n }\n \n+// ListTree returns the repo-relative paths of every file under prefix (a\n+// directory or a file path) at commit rev in the repository at dir, in git's\n+// order. A prefix that does not exist at rev gives an empty result. Like\n+// FileAt, dir must be